Directory: GENUS

The file GXDEMO.EXE located in the GENUS subdirectory is a
graphical, interactive demo of the GX Development Series by Genus
Microprogramming, Inc.

The minimum system requirements to run this demo are a 286-12MHz
IBM PC or compatible with at least 512 K of conventional memory
free, plus a VGA adapter and monitor. The demo will take
advantage of expanded or extended memory, and an SVGA adapter, if
present.

The demo was written using Borland C++ and the GX Series, but the
toolkits support Borland Pascal as well. Real, Protected Mode,
and Source Code versions of the toolkits are available.

Because of the intensive use of graphic image files, we strongly
recommend running the demo from a harddisk. To run the demo,
simply type 'GXDEMO'.
